*
* Bree's problem beyond the fibres: a thin tube under constant
* pressure and a cyclic temperature gradient through the wall,
* cycle by cycle with PASAPAS (Chapter 6, "The Bree vessel: period
* map and direct cyclic method"; companion exercise C6.1)
*
* STATUS: UNTESTED. Written against the operator notices; not run.
*
* Axisymmetric slice of an open tube, mean radius rm = 100 mm,
* wall e = 5 mm (e/rm = 0.05), height 1 mm, generalized plane
* strain (UZ = 0 at the bottom, UZ uniform at the top, free axial
* force). Temperature linear through the wall,
*   tau(r, t) = -tau0 x lambda(t),  x = (r - rm)/e,
*   lambda(t) = |sin t|, period pi.
* In this geometry the thermal stress is biaxial (hoop and axial),
* sigma_T = E alpha tau0 / (2 (1 - nu)), and the pressure stress is
* hoop only, sigma_P = p rm / e. With X = sigma_P / sY and
* Y = sigma_T / sY the regimes of the fibre model (Ch. 6) are
*   elastic X + Y <= 1; shakedown Y <= 2 and X + Y/4 <= 1;
*   alternating plasticity Y > 2 and X Y <= 1; ratchet otherwise.
* They are only approximate here (biaxial stress, finite wall):
* this is the point of the exercise. Fibre model, H = 0, case
* (X, Y) = (0.7, 1.5): ratchet of 0.3167 eY per cycle
* (python/examples/ch6/exo_bree_cyclic.py, eY = sY / E~).
*
* Data: E = 200 GPa, nu = 0.3, sY = 280 MPa, alpha = 1e-5 /K.
* Units: mm, MPa, K.  andrei.constantinescu@polytechnique.edu
*
* STEP 1  axisymmetric mesh of the wall, nr elements through it
*
  opti dime 2 mode axis elem qua4 echo 0;
  rm = 100.;  e = 5.;  h = 1.;  nr = 20;
  ri = rm - (e / 2.);  re = rm + (e / 2.);
  p1 = ri 0.;  p2 = re 0.;  p3 = re h;  p4 = ri h;
  bas  = droi nr p1 p2;  dro = droi 1 p2 p3;
  haut = droi nr p3 p4;  gau = droi 1 p4 p1;
  dom = dall bas dro haut gau;
*
* STEP 2  data of the case: X, Y, hardening H (0: perfect)
*
  xx = 0.7;  yy = 1.5;  hh = 0.;  ncyc = 10;  nstep = 40;
  you = 200000.;  nu = 0.3;  sy = 280.;  alp = 1.e-5;
  pr   = (xx * sy) * (e / rm);
  tau0 = ((2. * (1. - nu)) * (yy * sy)) / (you * alp);
  mess 'pressure ' pr ' MPa, tau0 = ' tau0 ' K';
*
* STEP 3  model: perfect or linear kinematic plasticity
*
  si (hh > 0.);
    mo = mode dom mecanique elastique isotrope
                  plastique cinematique;
    ma = mate mo 'YOUN' you 'NU' nu 'ALPH' alp 'SIGY' sy
                 'H' hh;
  sinon;
    mo = mode dom mecanique elastique isotrope plastique parfait;
    ma = mate mo 'YOUN' you 'NU' nu 'ALPH' alp 'SIGY' sy;
  finsi;
*
* STEP 4  generalized plane strain: UZ = 0 at the bottom, the top
*         stays plane (one common UZ, RELA ENSE) and carries no
*         axial force (open tube)
*
  aa = (bloq uz bas) et (rela ense uz haut);
*
* STEP 5  loads: constant pressure on the inner face, temperature
*         field tau(r) times lambda(t) = |sin t|
*
  fp = pres 'MASS' mo pr gau;
  pi0 = 3.141592653589793;
  ltt = (pi0 / nstep) * (prog 0. pas 1. (flot (ncyc * nstep)));
  lun = prog (dime ltt) * 1.;
  llam = abs (sin ((180. / pi0) * ltt));
  rr = coor 1 dom;
  rmc = manu 'CHPO' dom 1 'SCAL' rm;
  tau = exco ((-1. * (tau0 / e)) * (rr - rmc)) 'SCAL' 'T';
  t0 = 0. * tau;
  chp = char 'MECA' fp (evol manu 'TEMPS' ltt 'P' lun);
  cht = char 'T' tau (evol manu 'TEMPS' ltt 'LAMB' llam);
*
  tab = table;
  tab . 'MODELE' = mo;
  tab . 'CARACTERISTIQUES' = ma;
  tab . 'BLOCAGES_MECANIQUES' = aa;
  tab . 'CHARGEMENT' = chp et cht;
  ttem = table;
  ttem . 0 = t0;
  tab . 'TEMPERATURES' = ttem;
  tab . 'TEMPS_CALCULES' = ltt;
  pasapas tab;
*
* STEP 6  mean hoop strain u_r(rm)/rm at the end of every cycle
*         (lambda = 0: thermal strain zero), in units of eY
*
  pmid = bas poin 'PROC' (rm 0.);
  ey = sy / (you / (1. - nu));
  lc = prog;  le = prog;  ld = prog;
  eold = 0.;
  repeter bc ncyc;
    ii = &bc * nstep;
    urm = extr (tab . 'DEPLACEMENTS' . ii) 'UR' pmid;
    eth = (urm / rm) / ey;
    lc = lc et (prog (flot &bc));
    le = le et (prog eth);
    ld = ld et (prog (eth - eold));
    mess 'cycle ' &bc ': hoop strain ' eth ' eY, increment '
         (eth - eold);
    eold = eth;
  fin bc;
  dess (evol manu 'cycle' lc 'eps_t / eY' le);
*
* residual stress at the end of the last cycle, through the wall
  sg = chan 'CHPO' mo (tab . 'CONTRAINTES' . (ncyc * nstep));
  lr = prog;  lst = prog;  lsz = prog;
  repeter bn (nr + 1);
    pp = poin bas &bn;
    lr  = lr  et (prog (coor 1 pp));
    lst = lst et (prog (extr sg 'SMTT' pp));
    lsz = lsz et (prog (extr sg 'SMZZ' pp));
  fin bn;
  dess ((evol rouge manu 'r' lr 'sigma_t' lst)
     et (evol bleu  manu 'r' lr 'sigma_z' lsz));
*
  opti donn 5;
fin;
